  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The verbs: always at the end",
   "texto": [
    "The Japanese verb goes **al final** of the phrase and **no cambia con la persona**: **たべます** is «how», «Eat», «Eat», «We eat.»",
    "The educated form ends in **ます** (pronounced «mas», almost without the u). It serves the present and the future.",
    "To deny, **ます** changes to **ません**: **たべません** (not like). To ask, add **か**: **たべます か**."
   ]
